  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The corridor – handover and finish",
  "description": "A row of cones splits the court lengthways into two corridors. In one, a line (A) stands by the goal with all the balls and a line (B) at the other end. A dribbles to the middle of the court and hands the ball over to B, who is coming the other way. B takes the ball back towards the goal and shoots. A joins the back of line B, and B joins line A.\n\nUse the other corridor for two more lines (C and D) at the same time. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Leave the ball still right at the handover – no little taps."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The receiver arrives at speed and takes the ball straight on."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "High tempo in the runs."
    }
  ],
